## Analysis of Confirmed Metrics

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Underwriting performance (IGAAP, FY24):</strong> Star Health reported a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">combined ratio of 96.7%</span>, sub-100% and indicative of underwriting profitability on a full-year basis, driven by a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">claims ratio of 66.5%</span>. Notably, Q4 FY24 standalone combined ratio was reported at a tighter <strong>92.7%</strong>, suggesting improving loss experience into the back half of the year versus the full-year average.
</div>

- **Total GWP (IGAAP): ₹15,251 crore** for the year ended 31 March 2024 — the headline full-year gross written premium figure from the company's FY24 corporate presentation.
- **PAT (IGAAP): ₹845 crore** — full-year statutory profit after tax for FY24.
- **Retail health market share: 33.1%**, underscoring the company's <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">leadership position</span> in India's retail health insurance segment.
- **Solvency ratio: 2.21x** — comfortably above the IRDAI regulatory minimum of 1.50x, indicating adequate capital buffer.

